/** @page krb5security Security Notes

    - This module never logs secrets.
    - Password-based initial credential acquisition is noninteractive by default.
    - Initial credential acquisition supports FAST armor cache configuration.
    - Initial credential acquisition supports explicit enctype requests.
    - GSSAPI token inputs are validated before decoding.
    - GSSAPI initiator contexts default to the Kerberos mechanism.
    - GSSAPI contexts can use explicit credentials instead of process-global defaults.
    - GSSAPI channel bindings can be supplied explicitly for LDAP/TLS endpoint binding.
    - GSSAPI wrap/unwrap helpers support negotiated integrity and confidentiality layers.
    - Credential metadata APIs do not expose session-key or ticket bytes.
    - File-backed credential caches and keytabs honor Qore filesystem sandboxing.
    - Acquisition operations check cooperative cancellation before blocking calls.
    - Future releases will add keytab rotation APIs.
*/
